    "created_at": "2017-01-27T17:47:02Z",
    "updated_at": "2017-01-27T17:47:02Z",
    "body": "So what I propose\r\n\r\n1. Keep the `<menu>` element but only with the value that it adds,  allowing a context menu (via right click or slowtouch) to show up with application specific controls\r\n\r\n2. remove `<menuitem>`\r\n\r\n3. Extend `<button> <input type=\"checkbox\"> <input type=\"radio\">` to be used inside a menu\r\n\r\n4. Extend the `<details>` element with `role=\"drop-down-menu\"` or similar\r\n\r\n5. Allow customization of the action that opens a `<details>` (currently a click or touch) with `<details openwith=\"hover\">` or similar",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
